<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bobovac</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bobovac is a ruined royal fortress in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a>, near the town of Vareš. First recorded in the mid-14th century, it was a chief residence of the kings of Bosnia, several of whom were buried in its chapel. The Ottoman army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a> captured it in May 1463 after a short siege, a blow that led quickly to the fall of the Bosnian kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bobovac.jpg" alt="Bobovac" width="320" height="342" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnToni · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bobovac_9_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
